      "content_summary": "Explains how incorrect rate limit settings in Queue Manager prevent autoscaling triggers, resulting in resource exhaustion and slow response times.",
      "content_body": "When Queue Manager exhibits slow response times despite rising load, first verify that autoscaling policies are correctly configured to react to current metrics. A common root cause is a rate limit misconfiguration where the threshold for triggering scaling is set too high or is incompatible with the actual request volume. This leads to resource exhaustion as the instance count fails to increase in time. To resolve, review the current rate limit configuration and adjust it to align with expected traffic patterns. If necessary, request a capacity increase to provide a buffer while tuning the autoscaling parameters."
